d.R('**Health note:**',"**Health note:** finalised, sweep-confirmed and audit-governed through five audits. The overview's internal threads (fullness; \"in Him\"; the mystery thread; put off and put on) were confirmed by every dig. Audit 5 tested the overview's own architecture and took most of it down to size: the seams discarded, the summary unit and the Lukan affinities restricted, the frame kept at *moderate* in narrower terms. What rose is one anchor (Exod 6:6–8) and one local idiom (the Lukan idiom of 1:12–14). **The text-first count of what this letter does stays what it was: it argues by its own repeated words**, and the design language around those words is now better measured and more modest. Two limits remain on the pulpit side: the ESV wordings are from the US edition, and the 2:23 and 1:22 changes run against most of the commentators or rest on them, so both are flagged as open.")
